This is a common stage for early players.  Inventory management
is a crucial skill to learn.

> I have repeated potions, darts, and other stuff,
> with separate letters, so I can't pick up anything else. Is there a
> way to stack similar objects? (#adjust swaps letters instead, I
> haven't seen any other command).

As has been mentioned they need to be identical to stack.
They may be blessed, uncursed, cursed, have +0 or positive
or negative numbers.  A wand of cancelation will make them
all uncursed +0 and then they will all stack, but that's a
higher price than you likely want to pay.

> Also, sometimes things are stacked automatically (I have one pile with
> 3 darts and another one with 11). I don't know how to drop single
> items (or money for that matter), is that possible?

d1x

There's an interesting tradeoff - The biggest stacks are the
ones that are uncursed +0 but you still don't know it except by
the size of the stack.  The smallest stacks are the ones that are
both the best and the worst.

Your job is to learn how to tell cursed stuff and ditch them at the
stairs to keep the small stacks of the better items and learn to
identify them.  Your other job is to figure out what items really
are not worth carrying.  The majority of items types are worth
at most lugging to a stash.



